    "text": "To determine how many times Carrie charged her phone for the whole trip, we need to calculate the total distance she drove and then divide that by the distance at which she charges her phone. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Calculate the distance driven each day.\n   - First day: 135 miles\n   - Second day: 135 miles + 124 miles = 259 miles\n   - Third day: 159 miles\n   - Fourth day: 189 miles\n\n2. Find the total distance driven over the four days.\n   \\[\n   135 + 259 + 159 + 189 = 742 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n3. Determine how many times she charged her phone by dividing the total distance by the distance at which she charges her phone (106 miles).\n   \\[\n   \\frac{742}{106} = 7\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Carrie charged her phone \\(\\boxed{7}\\) times for the whole trip.",
